Z||000013||Monkeyman||11-08-2001||06:13 PM||||I can stand a few of the "older" songs/artists (mid '80s to early '90s), but for the most part, I can't really tolerate it for long.  I refuse to listen to any of the golden moldies of country.  Just not my taste.  I don't even know many of the new country artists names.  Most of the songs are the same anyway.  Some guys girlfriend/wife has left and taken his dog and pickup truck.  Now he's out of money and trying to get home.  Sooner or later, he'll end up in jail because he's jealous.  All he owns is a guitar, his jeans, a cowboy hat and (of course) a pick up truck.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I'm really not flaming anyone who's into country music.  We have (I think) a country music star here on the forum (at least he used to be).||||reg||1
